A few <em>MacRumors</em> readers informed us that after they turned off DoorDash notifications for offers specifically and then place a delivery order, the app will prompt users to re-enable notifications so they "never miss an order update," even though they still have notifications enabled for order updates. The wording of this prompt can trick users into thinking that they might not receive order updates, but tapping the button re-enables offers.<br/>
<br/>
A few more readers pointed out that the AliExpress app has been advertising in Live Activities, despite Apple's <a href="https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/live-activities/">app design guidelines</a> saying "don't use a Live Activity to display ads or promotions" under "best practices." Apple's App Store guidelines say apps should not send users "unsolicited messages" via Live Activities.<br/>
